 [; ── #976: the canonical image RE-PARSES to the SAME address ──
    in-a is a presentation variant, a leading comment plus line breaks and
    widened runs; in-b is the canonical image Family A pins. Hash-EQUAL is
    the round-trip closing: the head survives strict canonicalization and
    re-parses as the SAME element — not as text that merely looks like one,
    which is exactly what the stringifying heads used to produce. ]

 [case id=oph-201-plus-canonical-reparse level=core
  [tags operator-heads issue-976 roundtrip hash-pair]
  [in-a [#
[; presentation ]
[+
    5
    3]
#]]
  [in-b [#
[+ 5 3]
#]]
  [out-hash-eq [#
true
#]]
 ]

